{"ld": 1701, "paper": "HP1136", "session": "132", "title": "Resolve, Directing the Department of Education to Establish a Working Group to Study the Maine Learning Results (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "h-brennan-michael", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-cloutier-kristen", "h-dodge-janice", "h-gramlich-lori", "h-mitchell-christina", "h-moonen-matthew", "h-murphy-kelly", "s-rafferty-joseph", "h-sargent-holly"], "committee_code": "EDU", "committee_name": "Education and Cultural Affairs", "summary": {"text": "This bill creates the Learning Results Implementation Advisory Committee within the Department of Education to make recommendations on curricula, resources and staff training related to the study of racial and ethnic studies, financial literacy, civics and health care and to make recommendations on topics to be measured by learning indicators or to 4304 adjust learning indicators to reflect best practices. The bill appropriates $500,000 in fiscal 4315 year 2026-27 to provide grants to school administrative units and nonprofits to implement 4326 programs and learning activities based upon the committee's recommendation and appropriates funds for an Interdisciplinary Instruction Specialist position. The bill also directs the committee to include in the committee's recommendations the use of the department's online, open-source education platform that provides optional resources at no cost to educators in the State on topic areas and themes identified as areas of need by educators.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1136&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Finally Passed", "final_disposition": {"label": "Finally Passed", "date": "2025-06-13", "governor_action": "Signed", "governor_action_date": "2025-06-13"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "fiscal_note_url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/bills_132nd/fiscalpdfs/FN170102.pdf", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1701)